# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.
# Plan 00192 Task 3.3: `open` becomes a Go binary (src-go/cmd/open). The play installs the Go
# toolchain, builds the command from this checkout and installs it at ~/.local/bin/open in place
# of the bash script; the MIME and viewer packages are unchanged. Afterwards the owner checks
# SPEC-open.md section 7, H1-H5: `open --help`, a PDF opening in its default viewer, `open -a`
# showing the chooser with a Cancel row, `open -d` registering a default, and over SSH (or
# `open -t`) text, a directory, an image and a PDF opening in the terminal, Ctrl-C in less or
# mpv belonging to that program.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-cli-tools.yml


# Plan 00203 Task 3.13: rebuilds and installs ccy-teams, which now opens faster: the board's
# agent-bus calls (each checkout's seat list, each team's members, each person's Element
# sessions) run together instead of one after another, and the declare helper runs on
# /usr/bin/python3 instead of through the pyenv shim. The table and messages are unchanged. No
# ccy or image change; running sessions are not touched.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml

# Plan 00194 Task 2.0b: the goodbye host checks, automated (acceptance.bash; the plan has no
# triage.bash or deploy.bash). After play-claude-yolo.yml, so the sessions run the deployed
# image. It makes two throwaway teams, starts three idle ccy sessions on them in a scratch
# checkout on its own tmux server, ends one with Ctrl-C, one with podman stop and one by
# closing its window, counts the goodbye and disconnected messages each team gets, then removes
# all of it. Each launch runs ccy's normal startup clean-up, which removes every exited or
# created ccy container on the host (as any ccy launch does). The team purge relies on sudo
# staying cached (it does on this host). One sudo prompt.
00194-agent-bus-live-delivery-supervisor-plugin
